==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|hugjanan||think, consider|lang=gem-pro}}.  Cognate with Gothic [[𐌷𐌿𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽]], Old Norse [[huga]] (Icelandic [[hugsa]] ‘to think’).  Related to Middle Scots [[huik]] ‘regard, consider’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhyʤɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=weak|class=3}}

# to [[think]]
# to think about, to [[consider]]

